1. The Unified 3-Platform Blueprint for PenDone Data
To stay within three platforms while giving PenDone global scalability and BYOS storage:


1. Google AI Studio (Builder & Code Generator)
   * Generates your PenDone Store PWA shell, app manifest templates, HTML frontends, Code.gs scripts, and SQL schemas.
2. GitHub (Version Control, PWA Hosting & Deployment Automation)
   * Stores your PenDone Store and builder codebases, hosts the installable Progressive Web App (PWA) via GitHub Pages (which works across mobile and desktop browsers and installs like an app), and uses GitHub Actions to deploy updates automatically.
3. Supabase (Platform Database, Auth & Edge Functions)
   * Hosts PostgreSQL for PenDone's core metadata (users, app store listings, file pointers/permissions, and the 10% revenue ledger), handles user authentication, and runs Supabase Edge Functions as your metered API/gateway layer—while each user's Google Drive holds their per-app data files (data.json or Sheets) under drive.file OAuth permissions.
(Note: Code.gs stays a builder/app-level script option inside the PenDone ecosystem, while Supabase Edge Functions act as PenDone's reliable, scalable backend gateway so you aren't bottlenecked by Apps Script's 30-concurrent-execution ceiling.)


2. How Each Part of PenDone Works Together
